            "mimeType": "application/json",
            "compression": 0,
            "text": "{\"results\":[{\"kind\":\"issue\",\"owner\":{\"kind\":\"issue\",\"key\":\"CORE-1\",\"title\":\"Navigation instruments\",\"status\":\"triage\"},\"issue\":{\"key\":\"CORE-1\",\"title\":\"Navigation instruments\",\"status\":\"triage\"},\"id\":\"CORE-1\",\"snippet\":\"Navigation instruments\",\"rank\":0.004683840958798518,\"href\":\"/issues/CORE-1\"},{\"kind\":\"document\",\"owner\":{\"kind\":\"issue\",\"key\":\"CORE-1\",\"title\":\"Navigation instruments\",\"status\":\"triage\"},\"issue\":{\"key\":\"CORE-1\",\"title\":\"Navigation instruments\",\"status\":\"triage\"},\"artifact\":{\"slug\":\"spec\",\"name\":\"spec.md\"},\"id\":\"4bf56d5a-5c02-4031-9e20-fea770ef9e1b\",\"snippet\":\"Instruments\\n\\nThe \\u003cmark\\u003eastrolabe\\u003c/mark\\u003e measures altitude. Every \\u003cmark\\u003eastrolabe\\u003c/mark\\u003e is brass\",\"rank\":0.0027322405185855802,\"href\":\"/issues/CORE-1/spec?q=astrolabe\"},{\"kind\":\"ask\",\"owner\":{\"kind\":\"issue\",\"key\":\"CORE-1\",\"title\":\"Navigation instruments\",\"status\":\"triage\"},\"issue\":{\"key\":\"CORE-1\",\"title\":\"Navigation instruments\",\"status\":\"triage\"},\"id\":\"8106066f-d859-4f09-8f14-5627baa0be04\",\"snippet\":\"Where does the \\u003cmark\\u003eastrolabe\\u003c/mark\\u003e live between voyages? On the chart table In the captain\\u0026#39;s cabin Keep the \\u003cmark\\u003eastrolabe\\u003c/mark\\u003e on the chart table during\",\"rank\":0.0027322405185855802,\"href\":\"/issues/CORE-1/asks/8106066f-d859-4f09-8f14-5627baa0be04\",\"ask\":{\"state\":\"answered\",\"answer\":{\"user\":\"alice\",\"selected\":[\"On the chart table\"],\"text\":\"Keep the astrolabe on the chart table during every crossing, and recalibrate its rete against the meridian at local noon whenever the sky is clear enough to take a clean sighting. Log each reading beside the dead-reckoning position in the ship's book, note the observer and the instrument's serial number, and send any drift larger than half a degree to the instrument maker before the next voyage leaves port.\",\"at\":\"2026-11-11T11:42:07.235437Z\"}}},{\"kind\":\"comment\",\"owner\":{\"kind\":\"issue\",\"key\":\"CORE-2\",\"title\":\"Other work\",\"status\":\"triage\"},\"issue\":{\"key\":\"CORE-2\",\"title\":\"Other work\",\"status\":\"triage\"},\"id\":\"9cf85aab-ba6c-4063-a0a4-9488eebe7207\",\"snippet\":\"Move the \\u003cmark\\u003eastrolabe\\u003c/mark\\u003e diagram\",\"rank\":0.0014903130101375892,\"href\":\"/issues/CORE-2/comments/9cf85aab-ba6c-4063-a0a4-9488eebe7207\"}],\"total\":4,\"reachable\":4,\"limit\":20,\"offset\":0,\"took_ms\":37,\"degraded\":\"embedder_unavailable\",\"query\":{\"operators\":[],\"broadened\":false},\"filters\":{}}\n"
